Now that the tournament is over, I continued the game I started on my own
machine on October..

A knight with his horse, now on dungeon level 22.
I saw an unknown potion that according to my notes had base price of 
100 zorkmids. Confusion, extra healing, hallucination and restore ability
were the unknown ones in that group. None of them very dangerous, so I
quaffed it without further thought.
It turned out to be hallucination, and even though I am already on DL 22
I noticed I still didn't have an unihorn, so I just hallucinated.

I found a room that had items on most of the floor squares and some 
creature blocking the door. Hmm, sounds like a shop, so I decided not
to attack whoever it was on the doorway, and went on riding around the 
level.

In another room I saw a potion of sickness and quaffed it to get rid of
the hallucination.

In a corridor I met a purple worm that lunged forward and plucked me off
the saddled horse, then engulfed me. Some hits with the Excalibur and the
purple worm was no more.

I went back to the room looking like a shop and indeed it turned out to be 
a general store.

Now the weird part: the shopkeeper didn't welcome me in when I entered.
In fact, he didn't say ANYTHING at all! I don't remember ever before
in Nethack meeting a shopkeeper that doesn't greet a customer.
Sure, Budereyri tells me the prices of things when I #chat and blocks the
doorway if I carry something unpaid, but doesn't say anything when I walk
in from or out of the door.
What causes this? 
I would suspect that Budereyri is another Finn, but the name doesn't sound
Finnish :-)

